= Content Mods

This section catalogs all car and track mods in Assetto Maximus. Content mods are available from Wave 1 onward.

Mod entries follow this format: *Name* — Description. *Dependencies*. *Compatibility notes*.

== Cars

=== Wave 1 Cars — Spec & Open Wheel

- #link("https://www.overtake.gg/downloads/mazda-mx-5-global-cup-2016.6652/")[Mazda MX-5 Cup 2016] — Spec racing series car. Perfect for learning racecraft. *Dependencies: None*.
- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/caterham-seven-academy-2017.17001/")[Caterham Seven Academy 2017] — Two variants (LDH/RHD). Open-top spec racer with no assists. Excellent for building car control fundamentals.
- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/mini-cooper-jcw-uk-challenge-f56.30469/")[MINI Cooper JCW Challenge (F56) 2019] — Modern FWD spec-racer. Teaches front-wheel-drive dynamics and trail-braking.
- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/skip-barber-for-assetto-corsa.31943/")[Skip Barber F2000] — Tube-frame open-wheeler. The classic American racing school car — low power, high grip, teaches momentum driving.
- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/rsr-formula-3.8040/")[Dallara F312/F317 (Formula 3)] — Two cars covering the 2012 and 2017 F3 eras. High-downforce single-seaters for your first taste of proper downforce driving.

=== Wave 1 Cars — Touring & GT

- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/1999-nissan-primera-btcc.3828/")[Nissan Primera BTCC 1999] — Super Touring-era icon. Front-wheel-drive touring car with period-correct aero and racing pedigree.
- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/1998-bmw-320i-stw-btcc.32489/")[BMW E36 320i STW-BTCC 1998] — RWD touring car from the golden Super Touring era. Natural rival to the Primera.
- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/seat-leon-tcr-2018.20109/")[SEAT León TCR 2018] — Modern FWD touring car. TCR-spec aero and slicks with production-derived chassis.
- #link("https://www.overtake.gg/downloads/ferrari-488-gtlm-2017.35056/")[Ferrari 488 GTE] — GTE/GTLM endurance racer. Community conversion based on technical documentation. *Dependencies: None*.
- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/bentley-continental-gt3.6835/")[Bentley Continental GT3] — Thunderous GT3 racer. Massive presence on track, unique exhaust note.
- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/caterham-roadster-500.20619/")[Caterham Roadster 500 (fictional)] — A 500 bhp/tonne monster. Takes the Seven formula to its extreme limit.

=== Wave 1 Cars — Classics & Period

- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/abarth-turismo-competizione-berlina-corsa-1966.9721/")[Abarth 1000 TC Berlina Corsa 1966] — Four variants (Stock/Gr2/Gr5/Slalom). Tiny 1-litre rear-engined racer. Teaches momentum conservation on a shoestring budget.
- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/bmw-e30-touring.15812/")[BMW E30 325i Touring 1987] — Two variants (RWD/AWD). The classic boxy BMW wagon, ideal for casual track days and Nordschleife laps.
- #link("https://www.racedepartment.com/downloads/tvr-griffith-200.25994/")[TVR Griffith 200 1963] — Lightweight British V8 sports car. No ABS, no TC — raw analog driving.

